{"name":"Fireflies","hex":"#f6daa7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fireflies","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of firefly"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireflies"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fireflies (Owl City song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Fireflies\" is the 2009 debut single from American electronica project Owl City's album Ocean Eyes. It was released digitally on July 14, 2009, before it was serviced for radio airplay on September 1. Frontman Adam Young wrote the track about seeing fireflies in his hometown of Owatonna, Minnesota while he was awake with insomnia. Young produced the song alongside Matt Thiessen, who also provided guest vocals. The song is built around a \"bleepy\" synthline and includes lyrics about insomnia, fireflies and summer."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/Owlcity_fireflies_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireflies_(Owl_City_song)","wikidata":"Q1165917"},{"title":"Fireflies (Faith Hill album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fireflies is the sixth studio album by American country music singer Faith Hill. The album was released on August 2, 2005, via Warner Bros. Records Nashville. Her first album since her 2002 crossover album Cry, Fireflies marked a return to traditional country music for Hill. Hill co-produced the album with Byron Gallimore and Dann Huff. Husband Tim McGraw is featured on the single \"Like We Never Loved at All\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/57/Faithhillfireflies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireflies_(Faith_Hill_album)","wikidata":"Q3284910"},{"title":"Firefly","blocks":[{"text":"The Lampyridae are a family of elateroid beetles with more than 2,400 described species, many of which are light-emitting. They are soft-bodied beetles commonly called fireflies, lightning bugs, or glowworms for their conspicuous emission of light, mainly during twilight, to attract mates. The type species is Lampyris noctiluca, the common glow-worm of Europe. Light production in the Lampyridae is thought to have originated as a warning signal that the larvae were distasteful. This ability to create light was then co-opted as a mating signal and, in a further development, adult female fireflies of the genus Photuris mimic the flash pattern of the Photinus beetle to trap their males as prey."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Photuris_lucicrescens.jpg/330px-Photuris_lucicrescens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefly","wikidata":"Q25420"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif/500px-Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif/500px-Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALampyris_Noctiluca_(firefly)_mating.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Luciola4_crop.png/500px-Luciola4_crop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Luciola4_crop.png/500px-Luciola4_crop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A larviform female with light-emitting organs on her abdomen. Unlike larvae, she has compound eyes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALuciola4_crop.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Firefly_composite.jpg/500px-Firefly_composite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Firefly_composite.jpg/500px-Firefly_composite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photuris female by flash photography (above); by her own light (below)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirefly_composite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG/500px-Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG/960px-Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG/500px-Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg/500px-GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg/960px-GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg/500px-GluehwuermchenImWald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGluehwuermchenImWald.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Cantharis_lateralis_85974126.jpg/500px-Cantharis_lateralis_85974126.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","